Use APIexception(general-purpose custom exception) when something goes wrong in your business logic, but it's not about a missing resource.
Use Custom Exception when a specific resource (like a category, user, or product) is not found.

✅ Real-Life Analogy
Imagine you're running an e-commerce API:
ResourceNotFoundException → “Product with ID 91 not found” → clearly a missing thing
APIException → “Discount cannot be more than 100%” → the user did something illogical
They are both problems, but very different types of problems.


